{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: forecasts are systematically below realized prices by ~2–4 EUR for most of the 30-day horizon, especially during sustained uptrends.",
    "Trend underreaction / lag: when the market transitions into a rising regime, the forecast path follows the prior range and catches up too slowly (misses step-ups and higher highs).",
    "Volatility compression: forecast amplitude is too small—peaks are underpredicted and subsequent elevated levels are not maintained (true series stays high longer than forecast).",
    "Horizon effect: underprediction grows with lead time; errors are smaller in the first week and larger in weeks 2–4 as the model mean-reverts too aggressively.",
    "Post-spike behavior: after upward jumps, the model tends to fade the move (predicts pullback/sideways) while outcomes often continue drifting higher or plateau at a higher level."
  ]
}
